": 0.10235581253921024, \"vector_similarity\": 0.813835, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-17-Fix-Offset-Mismatch.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e97f16a48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-17-Fix-Offset-Mismatch.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-17-Fix-Offset-Mismatch.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1109, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:20\", \"token_count\": 617, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-27\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Validation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:04] Bob**: Ran the handshake validation under nominal latency — two nodes on the local network, dozens of connect attempts back to back. No failures.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:05] Evan**: Any dropped or retried handshakes at all?\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:30] Bob**: None. Every attempt authenticated cleanly on the first try at this latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:32] Diana**: We still need the high-latency case covered before this goes anywhere near the field.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:38] Bob**: Agreed, it's next on the list. First cut of the nominal-latency pass looks solid — leaving it in progress until we cover high latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:41] Diana**: Good.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 09:50] Diana**: Reopening this. Ran the handshake over a simulated high-latency link and it's timing out — never completes the exchange.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:08] Bob**: Timing out, or actively failing? Could just be the round trip budget being too tight.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:09] Diana**: Times out. And it gets worse the slower the link — feels like the handshake is doing more work per round trip than it should.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:18] Bob**: That tracks. The AES-256 pipeline we added on the output path adds per-packet overhead, and on a slow link that pushes the exchange past the timeout window. This depends on the encryption work settling down before we can retest — handshake work stays blocked for now.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 27 slack thread node sync handshak valid channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 09 22 2026 08 08 09 04 bob ran the handshak valid under nomin latenc two node on the local network dozen of connect attempt back to back no failur 2026 08 08 09 05 evan ani drop or retri handshak at all 2026 08 08 09 30 bob none everi attempt authent clean on the first tri at this latenc 2026 08 08 09 32 diana we still need the high latenc case cover befor this go anywher near the field 2026 08 08 09 38 bob agre it s next on the list first cut of the nomin latenc pas look solid leav it in progress until we cover high latenc 2026 08 08 09 41 diana good 2026 09 22 09 50 diana reopen this ran the handshak over a simul high latenc link and it s time out never complet the exchang 2026 09 22 10 08 bob time out or activ fail could just be the round trip budget be too tight 2026 09 22 10 09 diana time out and it get wors the slower the link feel like the handshak is do more work per round trip than it should 2026 09 22 1018 bob that track the ae 256 pipelin we ad on the output path add per packet overhead and on a slow link that push the exchang past the timeout window this depend on the encrypt work settl down befor we can retest handshak work stay block for now\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"id\": \"7c000945298cb210\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30989254185558235, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1306514997936891, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72812164, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1559, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:36\", \"token_count\": 450, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDiana walked the high-latency handshake timeout. The team left handshake work blocked; no timeout-bump workaround. Path still depends on the encryption workstream.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Handshake triage — nominal latency was fine; Bob's earlier validation held up on the local network. On a simulated high-latency link the handshake never finishes. It times out.\\n\\n**Bob**: That matches what I expected once we left the happy path. The prototype assumed round trips stay quick. High latency breaks the exchange.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Is this an encryption cost problem? AES-256 on the wire path is in the dependency chain here.\\n\\n**Bob**: It's related. The handshake still has to complete under that load, and on a slow link it doesn't. I don't have a fix that keeps the current exchange as-is.\\n\\n**Evan**: Bumping timeouts just hides it. If the link is slow enough, we still fail.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll leave the high-latency repro in place so we can re-check when encryption or the handshake design changes.\\n\\n**Alice**: Then we leave it. Handshake work stays blocked on timeouts under high latency. It depends on the encryption path, and we're not inventing a workaround in this meeting.\\n\\n**Bob**: Agreed — no timeout bump. We'll revisit when the crypto path moves.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari diana walk the high latenc handshak timeout the team left handshak work block no timeout bump workaround path still depend on the encrypt workstream sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript diana handshak triag nomin latenc wa fine bob s earlier valid held up on the local network on a simul high latenc link the handshak never finish it time out bob that match what i expect onc we left the happi path the prototyp assum round trip stay quick high latenc break the exchang charli is this an encrypt cost problem ae 256 on the wire path is in the depend chain here bob it s relat the handshak still ha to complet under that load and on a slow link it doesn t i don t have a fix that keep the current exchang ais evan bump timeout just hide it if the link is slow enough we still fail diana i ll leav the high latenc repro in place so we can re check when encrypt or the handshak design chang alic then we leav it handshak work stay block on timeout under high latenc it depend on the encrypt path and we re not invent a workaround in this meet bob agre no timeout bump we ll revisit when the crypto path move\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"id\": \"edcdc1df7188b1a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3089045393717771, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.13775785624539585, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7082468, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:18\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-47\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Title**: Async job scheduler for concurrent batch API work\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd an asynchronous job scheduler to the batch API for higher throughput under concurrent load. Async workers were added, but a concurrent I/O race was found to cut throughput by roughly 10%; the task is blocked, depending on the multi-threading work.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-47\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Title**: Async job scheduler for concurrent batch API work\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Async job scheduler processes batch API jobs concurrently without a throughput regression.\\n\\n- Concurrent I/O race condition is resolved (currently the blocking issue).\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-47\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Title**: Async job scheduler for concurrent batch API work\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd an asynchronous job scheduler to the batch API for higher throughput under concurrent load. Async workers were added, but a concurrent I/O race was found to cut throughput by roughly 10%; the task is blocked, depending on the multi-threading work.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-47\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Title**: Async job scheduler for concurrent batch API work\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-18**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because an async batch API scheduler is needed for higher throughput.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-25**: Diana - I/O Race Block (Blocked)\\n\\n - *Blocked after finding a concurrent I/O race that cuts throughput by roughly 10%, depending on the multi-threading work.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 47 sourc id src cu ciph 47 task id ciph 47 titl async job schedul for concurr batch api work status block assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 descript add an asynchron job schedul to the batch api for higher throughput under concurr load async worker were ad but a concurr i o race wa found to cut throughput by rough 10 the task is block depend on the multi thread work clickup task ciph 47 sourc id src cu ciph 47 task id ciph 47 titl async job schedul for concurr batch api work status block assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 accept criterion async job schedul process batch api job concurr without a throughput regress concurr i o race condit is resolv current the block issu clickup task ciph 47 sourc id src cu ciph 47 task id ciph 47 titl async job schedul for concurr batch api work status block assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 descript add an asynchron job schedul to the batch api for higher throughput under concurr load async worker were ad but a concurr i o race wa found to cut throughput by rough 10 the task is block depend on the multi thread work clickup task ciph 47 sourc id src cu ciph 47 task id ciph 47 titl async job schedul for concurr batch api work status block assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 activ histori 2026 08 18 alic task creat open open the task becaus an async batch api schedul is need for higher throughput 2026 08 25 diana i o race block block block after find a concurr i o race that cut throughput by rough 10 depend on the multi thread work\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e991efae8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"id\": \"cd124151c990e01e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.303731235570433, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09064162367204726, \"vector_similarity\": 0.80094033, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e991efae8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1019, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:06\", \"token_count\": 519, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Background: Path Fix Cleared Packaging\\n\\nBackslash path-handling defects that previously broke Windows builds were fixed on 2026-08-10, and a Windows build artifact was successfully produced by 2026-08-12. Packaging itself is no longer the blocker.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Current Blocker: Missing Code-Signing Certificate\\n\\nThe produced build artifact is unsigned, which triggers a SmartScreen warning and Defender flagging the binary as untrusted.\\n\\n- **Impact**: Site IT policies commonly block execution of unsigned/SmartScreen-flagged binaries outright, which would prevent installation on target deployment workstations without a manual security-policy override.\\n\\n- **Root Cause**: No code-signing certificate has been procured or configured in the Windows build pipeline yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-39\\n\\n# Compatibility Audit: Windows Build Signing Gap\\n\\n**Owner**: Evan\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2039\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n## Path to Resolution\\n\\nProcuring a code-signing certificate and wiring signing into the release build step is the only remaining item before this clears the T029 Windows compatibility gate — and, by extension, the T011 release checklist, which is holding on this exact signing gap alongside the T005 image slim-down.\\n\\n*Audit Status*: Active. Build produces successfully; signing certificate procurement is the sole open blocker.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 background path fix clear packag backslash path handl defect that previous broke window build were fix on 2026 08 10 and a window build artifact wa success produc by 2026 08 12 packag itself is no longer the blocker sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 current blocker miss code sign certif the produc build artifact is unsign which trigger a smartscreen warn and defend flag the binari a untrust impact site it polici common block execut of unsign smartscreen flag binari outright which would prevent instal on target deploy workstat without a manual secur polici overrid root caus no code sign certif ha been procur or configur in the window build pipelin yet sourc id src gdoc 39 compat audit window build sign gap owner evan document key doc 2039 last updat 2026 09 02 path to resolut procur a code sign certif and wire sign into the releas build step is the onli remain item befor this clear the t029 window compat gate and by extens the t011 releas checklist which is hold on this exact sign gap alongsid the t005 imag slim down audit status activ build produc success sign certif procur is the sole open blocker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"7d9dbdfb5b6d7c2f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30311436944244785, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1220091992034969, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7256931, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9aa652a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-02-Windows-Compatibility-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1340, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:48\", \"token_count\": 387, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-07\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Blocked on Upstream PDF Library\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-26\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:10] Charlie**: Bad news on the offset mismatch fix. It's definitely coming from `pdfminer.six`. There's an open issue on their repo for the whitespace handling we're hitting.\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:57] Alice**: Any workaround? We can't stay blocked on this forever.\\n\\n**[2026-06-26 09:58] Charlie**: Leaving it blocked for now. Local patches aren't getting us a clean fix — it's too deep in the parser.\\n\\n**[2026-08-05 14:18] Charlie**: Still watching upstream — there's a PR against pdfminer.six, #992, that should cover the whitespace fix, but it hasn't merged. No movement from the maintainers.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 15:58] Charlie**: Spent some time this week evaluating whether we fork pdfminer.six ourselves to get the fix in sooner.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 16:01] Alice**: What's the team's read on that?\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 17:55] Charlie**: We're passing on it. Maintaining a PDF parsing fork long-term is more risk than the wait. Staying blocked on #992.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:24] Charlie**: Checked again — #992 is still unmerged. No safe local path that doesn't involve owning a fork, so we're leaving the offset fix blocked pending the upstream merge.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Alice**: This is becoming a real risk for the v1.0 timeline.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Charlie**: Agreed, but I'd rather eat the delay than take on a parser fork we can't maintain.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 07 slack thread block on upstream pdf librari channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 26 last activ 2026 09 10 2026 06 26 09 10 charli bad news on the offset mismatch fix it s definit come from pdfminer six there s an open issu on their repo for the whitespac handl we re hit 2026 06 26 09 57 alic ani workaround we can t stay block on this forev 2026 06 26 09 58 charli leav it block for now local patch aren t get u a clean fix it s too deep in the parser 2026 08 05 14 18 charli still watch upstream there s a pr against pdfminer six 992 that should cover the whitespac fix but it hasn t merg no movement from the maintain 2026 08 20 15 58 charli spent some time this week evalu whether we fork pdfminer six ourselv to get the fix in sooner 2026 08 2016 01 alic what s the team s read on that 2026 08 2017 55 charli we re pass on it maintain a pdf pars fork long term is more risk than the wait stay block on 992 2026 09 1010 24 charli check again 992 is still unmerg no safe local path that doesn t involv own a fork so we re leav the offset fix block pend the upstream merg 2026 09 1010 41 alic this is becom a real risk for the v1 0 timelin 2026 09 1010 55 charli agre but i d rather eat the delay than take on a parser fork we can t maintain\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92c1abc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"id\": \"68389a2a4ecca69d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3000823233052108, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07976027615030115, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8141671, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92c1abc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-26-blocked-on-upstream.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1522, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:33\", \"token_count\": 462, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-58\\n\\n# Slack Thread: High-DPI Upstream Block\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:41] Diana**: Bad news on the high-DPI rendering fix. The rotation fix Charlie pushed works for simple cases, but it's completely breaking on documents with nested Form XObjects.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:43] Charlie**: Yeah, I looked into it. The underlying rendering library we're using (`pdf-lib-core`) has a known bug in how it handles coordinates for XObjects when a parent transform is applied.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:55] Alice**: Can we patch it?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 10:56] Charlie**: No.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:35] Charlie**: It's deep in their C++ core. I've opened an issue with the upstream maintainers, but they haven't responded.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:37] Evan**: We can't wait for an upstream fix if we're hitting the release gate. Can we work around it by flattening the PDFs first?\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 11:51] Charlie**: Flattening might work but it'll blow up the file size and we might lose some text layers.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:29] Alice**: @Diana, @Charlie, let's leave high-DPI rendering blocked for now. We need to decide if we can ship with this limitation or if we need a different rendering library entirely.\\n\\n**[2026-09-10 12:32] Diana**: Agreed. It only affects a small subset of complex documents, but we should document it as a known issue.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 58 slack thread high dpi upstream block channel cipherdoc date 2026 09 10 2026 09 1010 41 diana bad news on the high dpi render fix the rotat fix ch